Real defects the RED cycle found (not test bugs):
  * "Centaur Courser is not a spell": the engine refused to cast a vanilla
    creature because the catalog defines no spell spec for creatures with no
    rules text. Fixed with `CardDef::spell_spec()` (a vanilla creature is a
    permanent spell with no targets/effects, CR 608.3) and resolution now moves
    a permanent spell onto the battlefield instead of into a graveyard, with
    summoning sickness (CR 302.6). Regression test added:
    crates/core/tests/timing_mana.rs
    ::casting_a_creature_puts_it_onto_the_battlefield_with_summoning_sickness
  * self-play with the stub never attacked, which is exactly what the
    "self-play cast/attack counters" assertions are for.

