Increment 11 — live Decider-2B adapter: first real service interaction
The local service was already running (nothing was started or stopped).
Command: aperture-cli selfplay --seed 21 --decider-seat 0 --decider-timeout-ms 8000
         --max-steps 30 --out evidence/decider-probe.json

First probe (before the fix) — the real service answered once and then refused:
  decision_sources: {'decider-2b': 1, 'heuristic': 11, 'heuristic (decider fallback)': 8}
  policy_notes:
    "model decider-2b chose Keep hand (7 cards) (preference 0.600; not a win probability)"
    "decider-2b unavailable, used the heuristic: the service answered HTTP 422:
     {\"detail\":\"Choice decision requires 2 to 100 named criteria\"}"

Diagnosis: a single legal action was being sent as a one-option choice question,
which the typed readout rejects (verified against the live service, not assumed).
Fix: a single legal option is treated as `forced (single legal option)` — no call
is made and no spurious fallback is reported. Regression test:
  crates/ai/tests/decider.rs::a_single_legal_option_is_forced_and_never_asked_of_the_model
  test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed

After the fix (150 decisions, seed 21, seat 0):
  decision_sources: {'decider-2b': 12, 'forced (single legal option)': 65, 'heuristic': 73}
  notes: real answers with preferences 0.600 / 0.412 / 0.708 / 0.658 (choice
  concentration, not win probability); the 73 'heuristic' entries are the other
  seat, which is heuristic by design; zero fallbacks.
Report: evidence/decider-probe.json

Provider response stability (observed, two fetches seconds apart):
  fetch1 sha256 892ba7b629778514 len 99148
  fetch2 sha256 4df376dcc74fe163 len 99148
  top-level keys that differ between two fetches: ['viewCount']  (139 vs 140)
  card-entry fields that differ: [] count 0
So the report's sha256 identifies the fetched bytes, not a stable provider blob.

